ssing\".  \n\n==Ingredients==\n*⅔ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Ketchup|ketchup]]\n*¾ cup white [[Cookbook:Granulated Sugar|granulated sugar]]\n*½ cup white [[Cookbook:Wine vinegar|wine vinegar]]\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]] \n*2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n*2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Combine all ingredients in a [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]] or [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]], and process until smooth. The goal is to have a smooth red/orange sauce.\n#Pour the sauce into a bowl and chill covered in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes prior to use.\n\n==Notes, tips and variations==\n* Instead of using the blender, you can whisk the ingredients in a bowl.\n\n==Warnings==\n* Keep refrigerated\n\n[[Category:Californian recipes|French Dressing]]\n[[Category:Recipes for salad dressing|French Dressing]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ketchup]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"French Dressing","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"⅔ cup ketchup","sourceText":"⅔ cup ketchup","amountText":"⅔ cup ketchup","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¾ cup white granulated sugar","sourceText":"¾ cup white granulated sugar","amountText":"¾ cup white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ cup white wine vinegar","sourceText":"½ cup white wine vinegar","amountText":"½ cup white wine vinegar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ cup vegetable oil","sourceText":"½ cup vegetable oil","amountText":"½ cup vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"¼ cup minced onion","sourceText":"¼ cup 